  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>EtOK is potassium ethylene oxide and it is colourless gas and is liquid at low temperatures and is highly flammable i.e. that catches fire easily and undergoes alkylation reactions with many organic compounds and EtOH is the ethanol.</p><p>The heating&nbsp;of 2-chloro-1-phenylbutane&nbsp; with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>EtOK</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>EtOH</mi></math>gives&nbsp;X&nbsp;as the major product. Reaction&nbsp;X&nbsp;with&nbsp;H<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>OAc</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>followed by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaBH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gives&nbsp;Y&nbsp;as the major product.&nbsp;Y&nbsp;is 1-phenylbutanol.</p><p><img height=\"178\" src=\"assets\\st0167_0b94ab8e4656.png\" width=\"972\" /></p>"
  }
